From 5716d312933083d88dce885b7afd1e8e7666e8f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:38:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(posting): the index swing judges the swept work against
 the standing steel

As a work-turning A indexes, the stock, parts and turning fixtures it
sweeps are now judged against the face the rotary stands on (the machine
file's new axis_to_table, its centre height; the microARC 4 states
3.15 in) and against every fixed fixture over the work's X span, by its
box's distance from the line. A strike refuses the post naming the op,
the index and the steel; a machine with no figure, a fixture with no
facets or one reaching across the line is named in the gate's
not-judged line, never skipped in silence.

Fixes #1107

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
